{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Issachar, a strong-boned donkey</b> — qere in it חמור גורם, that Leah heard the sound of the donkey's cry and went out to meet Jacob and brought him to her tent:" "<b>between the saddlebags</b> — two times in the Masorah: here and the other למה ישבת בין המשפתים. Just as the donkey bears every burden, so Issachar bore the burdens of Israel in Torah, and the majority of the Sanhedrin were from Issachar. Written here: רובץ בין המשפתים — that they would rest Torah upon Israel in the Chamber of Hewn Stone, which was half in the sacred and half in the profane. And written there: למה ישבת בין המשפתים — that his inheritance was on the shore of the sea, for [the word] means shore to dry land, as we translate [in Aramaic] ואחסנתיה בין תחומיא:"], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {1 "The phrase 'בי [ן ים ליבשה' appears corrupt; the bracketed letter is uncertain. Translated hyper-literally as 'for [the word] means shore to dry land,' reading the Aramaic cognate for shore/boundary as the implied etymology. The Aramaic citation 'ואחסנתיה בין תחומיא' is from Targum Jonathan to Judges 5:16."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:18:48.301187159Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}